      "summary": {
        "unit_id": "hmh07-lua-follow6:114",
        "answer": "Takes menu f1_arg0, controller f1_arg1 and eight layout bounds f1_arg2..f1_arg9; calls LUI.UIElement.new and sets the literal class/id/sound. Creates the empty HeroAbilityUseString label with its literal color, font, material, spacing and alignments. A PerController heldWeapons.0.updateWeaponSelect subscription asks PulseElementToStateAndBack(self, Respawn, controller); the callback does not use the delivered model. There is no weapon-name lookup in this selected body. Exact child order: HeroAbilityUseString. All layout/property/asset values and each callback body are retained in the ordered trace. Calls the optional same-file-or-unresolved PostLoadFunc at its exact source position, then returns self; a same name in another file supplies no binding. Base/child lifetime, model/event/animation delivery and native asset behavior remain external unless a reused exact provider contract explic [excerpt; exact source record identified separately]",
        "unknowns": [
          "Effective HMH settings/data/assets, true load/overwrite/class lookup order, original recovered-text fidelity, native callback delivery and service/server implementations remain open.",
          "Independent correctness review and final game tests remain deferred."
